From 2e0d5457a19782d1e4c44f86b1b79a13e274c28e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:10:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camera: the IMX585 readout check accepts the original driver
 and checks the auto config like the IMX477

Why: After configure() the colour IMX585 block compared ScalerCropMaximum
with the table row's active size times the binning. The original Apertar
imx585 driver (e5b74d3) reports a binned mode's crop as the output size
(1920x1080 at 0,0 for 1080p, imx585.c:803-808 and :2379-2381@e5b74d3),
and libcamera sets ScalerCropMaximum from that analogCrop on every
configure (pipeline_base.cpp:568). So every binned mode, 1080p included,
is refused (confirmed in code, not run on a Pi). The block also did not
tell an explicit sensor config from an auto one. Colour IMX585 has no
auto fallback yet (commit 5 brings back 1.6.0's,
CameraController.cpp:5993-5996@upstream-1.6.0), and 1.6.0 checks an auto
config with the IMX477/577 size rule (invalidReadout,
CameraController.cpp:6166-6168@upstream-1.6.0: same raw width, height at
least the requested height).

What: The exact-mode block runs only for an explicit sensorConfig. Its
crop comparison is skipped when the reported crop equals the configured
raw size, because such a driver gives no window to compare. A colour
IMX585 on the auto path gets the IMX477/577 size rule. That half does
nothing yet: it takes effect only when commit 5 adds the colour IMX585
3840-wide crops to allowAutoSensorConfigFallback. It is new compared with
1.6.0, whose IMX585 auto fallback had no readout check at all
(CameraController.cpp:6162-6164@upstream-1.6.0 lists only IMX477/577/294).
It is the rule from the design page, taken from the IMX477/577 one. Mono
is unchanged (it always configures auto and never had a readout rule).

Tested: check_core.sh both builds (libcamera and without) and the host
tests pass. Needs the camera. Original driver: Core starts at 1920x1080
and the output of
journalctl -u apertar-core -b | grep -E 'camera configured|adjusted by the driver'
no longer has "adjusted by the driver (scaler crop maximum (0, 0)/1920x1080)"
(before this commit that line settles the refusal). Port driver (cd548ef):
the "camera configured:" lines for 1920x1080, 3840x2160 and 3840x2072 are
the same as before. The auto-path rule is covered by the commit 5 check:
on the port driver a 3840x2076 auto request is refused with
"adjusted to too-small stream 3840x2072".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/camera/CameraController.cpp | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/camera/CameraController.cpp b/src/camera/CameraController.cpp
index 784719a..701b9c2 100644
--- a/src/camera/CameraController.cpp
+++ b/src/camera/CameraController.cpp
@@ -8475,7 +8475,8 @@ private:
 
                 if (includeRawStream &&
                     (sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx477 || sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx577 ||
-                     sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx294)) {
+                     sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx294 ||
+                     (sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx585 && !monochromeSensor_ && !useExplicitSensorConfig))) {
                     const libcamera::StreamConfiguration &candidateRawConfig =
                         candidateConfig->at(rawStreamIndex);
                     const bool invalidReadout = sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx294
@@ -8496,10 +8497,10 @@ private:
                     }
                 }
 
-                if (sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx585 && !monochromeSensor_) {
-                    // A colour IMX585 is configured explicitly, so the driver must hand over exactly the
-                    // mode asked for: raw size, bit depth, and a ScalerCropMaximum of active size x binning
-                    // (the window the driver reports in native pixels). A mode it adjusted is refused.
+                if (sensorFamily_ == SensorFamily::Imx585 && !monochromeSensor_ && useExplicitSensorConfig) {
+                    // Configured explicitly, a colour IMX585 driver must hand over exactly the mode asked
+                    // for: raw size, bit depth, and a ScalerCropMaximum of active size x binning (the
+                    // window the driver reports in native pixels). A mode it adjusted is refused.
                     std::string adjusted;
                     if (includeRawStream) {
                         const libcamera::StreamConfiguration &candidateRawConfig =
@@ -8526,7 +8527,8 @@ private:
                     const auto *imx585Row = apertar::imx585::find(imx585Class, sanitized.resolution.width,
                                                                   sanitized.resolution.height, 0);
                     const auto cropMaximum = camera_->properties().get(libcamera::properties::ScalerCropMaximum);
-                    if (adjusted.empty() && imx585Row && cropMaximum) {
+                    // A driver that reports its crop as the output size gives no window to compare.
+                    if (adjusted.empty() && imx585Row && cropMaximum && cropMaximum->size() != rawSize) {
                         const uint32_t binning = imx585Row->binned ? 2u : 1u;
                         if (cropMaximum->width != imx585Row->width * binning ||
                             cropMaximum->height != imx585Row->height * binning)
